<title>USA: Black &amp; Decker Corp Q1 oper shr falls.</title>
<headline>Black &amp; Decker Corp Q1 oper shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>TOWSON, Md. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.27		    $0.35</p>
<p> Oper income	     26,300		   34,600</p>
<p> Revs		   1,105,000		1,065,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  96,200		   89,500</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q1 oper earnings exclude gain of $70.4 million or $0.79 a share on sale of PRC, and a restructuring charge of $67.0 million, or $0.75 a share. Including these items, 1996 Q1 earnings were $0.39 a share.</p>
<p>EPS figures are for both primary and fully diluted shares. The shares used in computing earnings per share are for fully diluted shares.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected 1997 Q1 earnings of $0.26 a share, according to First Call.</p>
</text>
